This is a fork of an existing open source project with some custom functionality that was implemented for my use. Document the general status of each of them here to expedite future merge conflicts and to harden against future changes. When creating a new feature, make sure to add it to `.cursor\rules\my-update.mdc` and keep it up to date 

1. **Chat History / Reverse Search (Ctrl+R)**
   - **Feature**: Terminal-style reverse incremental search for previously sent messages. Press `Ctrl+R` in the chat input to open a popup showing message history. Type to filter results in real-time. Arrow keys or scroll to navigate, Enter to select.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/chathistory/ChatHistoryManager.hpp/.cpp` - Singleton managing per-channel message history with persistence to `Misc/chat-history.json`. Stores up to 5000 messages per channel, deduplicates consecutive identical messages, and provides filtered search.
     - `src/widgets/splits/MessageHistoryPopup.hpp/.cpp` - Popup UI for displaying and navigating history with search term highlighting.
     - `src/widgets/splits/MessageHistoryItem.hpp/.cpp` - Custom list item for rendering messages with highlighted search matches.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/Application.hpp/.cpp` - Added `ChatHistoryManager` singleton initialization and `getChatHistoryManager()` accessor.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitInput.hpp/.cpp` - Added `historySearchMode_`, `openMessageHistory()`, `updateHistoryPopup()`, `hideHistoryPopup()`, `exitHistorySearch()` methods. Modified `eventFilter()` to handle search mode keyboard events. Modified `postMessageSend()` to record messages to history.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Changed default `Ctrl+R` from "changeChannel" (now `Ctrl+Shift+R`) to "openMessageHistory".
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added "openMessageHistory" action definition.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added new source files.
     - `mocks/include/mocks/EmptyApplication.hpp` - Added mock for `getChatHistoryManager()`.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - History saves every 60 seconds and 5 seconds after the last message sent.
     - Popup shrinks to fit content (minimum 1 row, maximum 7 rows).
     - Current text in input is preserved when opening/closing search.
     - Non-contiguous duplicate messages are collapsed when filtering.

2. **Chat Control / Crowd Copy (Per-Split Ctrl+D Toggle)**
   - **Feature**: Per-split chat control mode that predicts a likely crowd message from recent chat and prefills the split input.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/crowdcopy/CrowdCopyEngine.hpp/.cpp` - Stateless evaluator for predicted message selection.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitInput.hpp/.cpp` - Added chat control state/timers, prediction updates, toggle handling, lock input behavior, mutual exclusion with reverse search, and visual active indicator.
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Added split-level crowd copy mode getters/setters and persistence plumbing.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added `toggleCrowdCopy` action.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Added default `Ctrl+D` keybind.
     - `src/singletons/Settings.hpp` - Added tunable crowd-copy settings.
     - `src/widgets/settingspages/GeneralPage.cpp` - Added Crowd Copy settings section in preferences.
     - `src/common/WindowDescriptors.hpp/.cpp` - Added split descriptor field for persisted crowd copy mode.
     - `src/singletons/WindowManager.cpp` - Save/load of split crowd copy mode.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitContainer.cpp` - Apply persisted crowd copy mode on restore.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added crowd copy sources.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Toggle is restricted to normal Twitch channel splits (`Twitch`/`TwitchWatching`) and ignored in non-channel/special splits.
     - Prediction uses time decay and per-user dedupe, is capitalization-agnostic for grouping, and preserves dominant capitalization variant for display.
     - Only ordinary user chat is scored. Channel-point redeems, highlighted redeems, announcements, watch streaks, notifications, and other non-chat events are ignored so redeem floods cannot dilute or starve a winner.
     - Initial winner can be immediate; later winner changes require confirmation window plus blank buffer before swap.
     - Prediction loop runs only for visible split tabs and analyzes a capped recent **user-message** count (`crowdCopyMaxMessagesToAnalyze`, default 100), over-fetching the snapshot so ignored events do not consume the cap.
     - While chat control is enabled, input is read-only and is cleared on disable.
     - `Ctrl+R` and chat control are mutually exclusive; reverse search activation is swallowed while chat control is on.
     - Reverse search now toggles closed on repeated `Ctrl+R`, with explicit handling to avoid shortcut routing issues.
     - One-time completion popup suppression is applied for initial autofill so Enter send is not interrupted.

3. **Channel Points Popup / Queueing**
   - **Feature**: Split-scoped popup for Twitch channel point rewards, opened from the split header or hotkey, backed by a local websocket service (`localhost:8765`) rather than Twitch directly.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsModels.hpp` - Local DTO/view-state structs for rewards, cooldown/limit metadata, and popup rendering state.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsClient.hpp/.cpp` - Websocket payload builder/parser for `replace_subscriptions`, `get_channel_points`, `get_rewards`, and `redeem`.
     - `src/controllers/channelpoints/ChannelPointsController.hpp/.cpp` - Application-owned controller managing connection lifecycle, per-channel state, queue modes, throttling, and reward event handling.
     - `src/widgets/splits/ChannelPointsPopup.hpp/.cpp` - Popup UI showing balance, rewards, queue state, favorites, and controls.
     - `src/widgets/splits/ChannelPointsConfirmDialog.hpp/.cpp` - Confirm dialog shown before manual redeem with Shift-to-keep-open behavior.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/Application.hpp/.cpp` - Added `ChannelPointsController` singleton initialization and `getChannelPoints()` accessor.
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Added `openChannelPointsPopup()` and split hotkey action wiring.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitHeader.hpp/.cpp` - Added split-header entry point for channel points.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added `showChannelPoints` action definition.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/HotkeyController.cpp` - Added default `Ctrl+Alt+P` binding.
     - `src/singletons/Settings.hpp` - Added persistent favorites storage for pinned rewards.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added channel-points controller and popup sources.
     - `mocks/include/mocks/EmptyApplication.hpp` - Added mock accessor for `getChannelPoints()`.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Popup is bound to the current Twitch split channel and only subscribes while visible; closing or hiding it unsubscribes from that channel.
     - UI includes current point balance, manual redeem with confirm dialog, queue-once mode, repeat mode, emergency clear, and per-reward pin/favorite support.
     - Manual confirm supports Shift to keep the popup open after redeem.
     - Confirm-dialog input highlights characters past Twitch's 500-character soft limit with yellow foreground text and a live over-limit counter.
     - Queue logic lives in the controller with one in-flight redeem per reward, 3-second minimum repeat interval, and deduped one-shot arming.
     - Success sound is played only after a confirmed successful `redeem_result`.
     - Popup refresh is local/timer-driven for cooldown expiry so rewards can unlock without requiring a full websocket snapshot refresh.
     - External reward-redemption events only force a snapshot refresh for rewards with global limits/cooldowns; ordinary user redeems are otherwise ignored for UI refresh.

4. **Over-Length Twitch Message Display**
   - **Feature**: Incoming Twitch chat messages longer than Twitch's normal 500-character limit display the extra text instead of visually losing it. Characters after 500 are rendered as readable black text with a yellow background.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/messages/MessageBuilder.hpp/.cpp` - Detects over-limit incoming message content, builds the first 500 characters normally, and appends the suffix as highlighted overflow text.
     - `src/messages/MessageElement.hpp/.cpp` - Added optional per-text-element background color support.
     - `src/messages/layouts/MessageLayoutElement.hpp/.cpp` - Paints optional text-element backgrounds behind highlighted overflow text.
     - `src/providers/twitch/ChannelPointReward.hpp/.cpp` - Preserves redemption `user_input` from PubSub/EventSub payloads.
     - `src/providers/twitch/TwitchChannel.cpp` - Uses PubSub/EventSub `user_input` to hydrate queued channel-point reward messages when it extends the IRC text.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Full message text remains in `messageText` and `searchText`.
     - Twitch emote parsing is preserved for the normal first 500 characters; the overflow suffix is rendered as plain highlighted text so the hidden payload remains readable.
     - Splits in the middle of a word avoid inserting an artificial space at the 500-character boundary.
     - Custom reward input normally enters as a `PRIVMSG` with `custom-reward-id`; PubSub/EventSub provides a richer redemption object with `user_input`, which can contain text not visible in the IRC payload.

5. **Chat Font Fallbacks for Special Characters**
   - **Feature**: Chat text uses explicit fallback families so special characters not covered by the selected chat font can still render.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/singletons/Fonts.cpp` - Appends globally installed fallback families to chat font family lists after Chatterino normalizes the selected font.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Applies only to chat-style fonts (`ChatSmall` through `ChatVeryLarge`), covering message text, usernames, and split input without changing UI fonts.
     - `Gadugi` is included for Canadian Aboriginal Syllabics such as `ᗍᐈᐈᐈᐈ`, which FreeSerif does not cover.
     - `FreeSerif` remains included for other special characters.
     - If Qt does not already see a fallback family, the Windows font registry is used to load the installed font file with `QFontDatabase::addApplicationFont()`.

6. **Per-Split Input Box Toggle**
   - **Feature**: Individual splits can automatically hide their empty input box to reclaim vertical chat space.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Added per-split hidden-input state, automatic visibility updates, focus/reply handling, hotkey wiring, and popup/descriptor plumbing.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitHeader.cpp` - Added a checkable `Hide input box` action to the split's `More` menu.
     - `src/controllers/hotkeys/ActionNames.hpp` - Added the configurable `toggleInputVisibility` split action without a default binding.
     - `src/common/WindowDescriptors.hpp/.cpp` - Added the persisted `inputHidden` split descriptor field.
     - `src/singletons/WindowManager.cpp` - Retains upstream descriptor-based split serialization after resolving the feature rebase.
     - `src/widgets/splits/SplitContainer.cpp` - Restores hidden-input mode for persisted splits.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Hidden inputs remain constructed but use the existing zero-height `SplitInput::hide()` path, avoiding layout and paint cost while retaining keyboard event routing.
     - The input automatically appears when it has text, enters reverse search, receives focus, or starts a reply; it hides again when empty and unfocused.
     - The toggle is stored per split and copied when a split is opened in a popup window.

7. **Raid Follow Banner**
   - **Feature**: When a watched channel starts an outgoing raid, visible splits show a banner with target info, Streamlink / go-to-tab actions, and an auto-follow checkbox. Chat also gets started / gone-through / cancelled system messages.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/providers/twitch/RaidInfo.hpp` - Shared raid payload / UI state structs.
     - `src/providers/twitch/pubsubmessages/Raid.hpp/.cpp` - Parser for PubSub `raid_update_v2` / `raid_go_v2` / `raid_cancel_v2`.
     - `src/widgets/splits/RaidBannerWidget.hpp/.cpp` - Banner UI stacked under the pinned-message banner.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/providers/twitch/PubSubManager.hpp/.cpp` - `listenToRaid()` and raid signals.
     - `src/providers/twitch/PubSubClient.cpp` - Dispatch `raid.{channelID}` messages.
     - `src/providers/twitch/PubSubMessages.hpp` - Export raid message parser.
     - `src/providers/twitch/TwitchChannel.hpp/.cpp` - Raid listen, state, Helix target-stream fetch, system messages.
     - `src/providers/twitch/TwitchIrcServer.cpp` - Route PubSub raid signals onto the channel.
     - `src/widgets/splits/Split.hpp/.cpp` - Insert `raidBanner_` between pinned banner and chat view.
     - `src/CMakeLists.txt` - Added new sources.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Banner is shown only when the split is on-screen (`QWidget::isVisible()`), including unfocused windows; background tabs are ignored.
     - First `raid_update_v2` per raid id posts "X started a raid to Y." Countdown ticks do not repeat that message.
     - Banner countdown is anchored to the first update's `force_raid_now_seconds`; later PubSub ticks keep that origin because Twitch repeats a fixed 90s value.
     - `raid_go_v2` / `raid_cancel_v2` post "gone through" / "cancelled" messages in the source channel, once per raid (Twitch can emit go multiple times).
     - Raid system-message names are clickable UserInfo links, matching live/offline/hosting notices.
     - Auto checkbox starts unchecked for each raid and only stays checked if the user clicks it. When checked, the banner jumps to an existing target split or opens a new main-window tab when the raid executes, once per raid from a visible split.

8. **TwitchPipe stream player backend**
   - **Feature**: External Tools has a Stream player choice between Streamlink and TwitchPipe. TwitchPipe has its own path, quality, config file, and extra options. Choose quality runs `twitchpipe --streams` and reuses the existing quality popup.
   - **Files Modified**:
     - `src/singletons/Settings.hpp` - `StreamPlayerBackend` and `TwitchPipeQuality` settings, plus magic_enum display names for the TwitchPipe quality values.
     - `src/util/StreamLink.hpp/.cpp` - Backend-aware binary path, not-found dialog, process setup, `--streams` listing, and argument building. `openStreamlink` and `openStreamlinkForChannelOrUrl` stay the public API.
     - `src/widgets/dialogs/QualityPopup.cpp` - `showDialog` sorts the option list before filling the combo box.
     - `src/widgets/settingspages/SettingWidget.hpp/.cpp` - `conditionallyEnabledBy(EnumStringSetting<T>&, T)` and dropdown instantiations for the new enums.
     - `src/widgets/settingspages/ExternalToolsPage.cpp` - Stream player section with a backend dropdown and Streamlink / TwitchPipe groups. The page uses `SettingsPage::managedConnections_` for the enable binding.
     - `tests/CMakeLists.txt` - Registers `tests/src/StreamLink.cpp`.
   - **Files Added**:
     - `src/util/StreamQualitySort.hpp/.cpp` - `sortStreamQualities` ranks Choose-popup labels for both backends.
     - `tests/src/StreamLink.cpp` - Order checks for Choose-popup quality labels.
   - **Behavior Notes**:
     - Quality listing runs `twitchpipe --log-level error --streams <channel>`, optionally with `--config` when the config path is set. Each non-empty stdout line is one quality. Streamlink still parses the `Available streams:` line and strips its ` (best)` / ` (worst)` markers before the popup sees the names.
     - Both Choose popups run that list through `sortStreamQualities` in `QualityPopup::showDialog`. Resolution labels go highest height first, and a higher frame rate breaks a tie (`1080p60` before `1080p`, `720p60` before `720p`). A trailing ` (...)` suffix such as ` (source)` is ignored for rank and kept on the selectable string. `best` is first, unrecognized labels keep their relative order, `worst` follows those, and `audio`, `audio_only`, and `audio-only` are last. Duplicate labels are kept.
     - Non-zero exit posts the last stderr line as a system message on the split that started the launch, and logs a warning. Offline channels typically end with `Error: no streams found on channel X`.
     - A bare login is passed through. A URL with no scheme, including `twitch.tv/<name>`, gets `https://` prepended. That rewrite also happens inside `openStreamlink` when TwitchPipe is the backend at launch time, so the quality popup follows the backend selected when OK is clicked.
     - Preferred quality maps to `best`, no quality argument (config priority list), or the custom priority string. An empty custom list falls back to `best`. Popup quality names are passed through unchanged, including labels like `1080p60 (source)`.
     - `--config` is sent only when the config file setting is non-empty. Otherwise TwitchPipe uses its own lookup, next to the executable and then the working directory.
     - A normal Streamlink launch still gets the same arguments. The chat system message is `Opening <channel> in Streamlink ...` or `Opening <channel> in TwitchPipe ...`.
     - Attached quality queries are deleted when they exit. FailedToStart shows one not-found dialog and deletes the process. Detached launches use `startDetached`, show that dialog only from the false return, and delete the `QProcess` without waiting for the player to exit.
     - Holding Shift while starting a launch with quality `Choose` skips the popup and uses `best` for both backends. Hotkeys whose binding lacks Shift will not fire with Shift held, so menu and button triggers are the intended path.
     - The menu label "Open in streamlink", the `/streamlink` command, and the `openInStreamlink` hotkey id are unchanged.

